<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Somerled</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 1164</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Somhairle</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Somerled was a Norse-Gaelic warlord of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argyll">Argyll</a> who married a daughter of Olaf I, king of Mann and the Isles. In 1156 he defeated his brother-in-law Godred in a sea battle and took the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrides">Hebrides</a>, and by 1158 he held the whole kingdom for a time. He was killed at Renfrew in 1164 while invading <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>, and his descendants included the MacDougalls and the MacDonald Lords of the Isles.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/somerled.jpg" alt="Somerled" width="320" height="108" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Somairle_mac_Gilla_Brigte_(Cambridge_Corpus_Christi_College_139,_folio_ar).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
